Templates that kill the reference process with a Go stack overflow (fatal
error, not recoverable) or never finish. They never run through hbref;
TestRefFatal requires an error from the candidate (render or limit), not a
crash. Contexts are {} unless a .json section gives one.

unless-in-with, equal-in-each, select-sexpr-in-if, if-in-if and
with-in-each are the same loop through Fn instead of Inverse: the helper
evaluates the enclosing block's program, which holds the call. unless-in-with, equal-in-each and if-in-if
overflow the Go stack within seconds; select-sexpr-in-if had not finished
after 5 minutes, and with-in-each after 1 minute.

unless-in-inverse needs a truthy t: with {} the reference renders "" (unless
calls Fn, and the {{^x}} block has no program), which the engine matches.
With t true, unless calls Inverse, which re-enters the enclosing {{^x}}
inverse forever: the reference overflows the Go stack, and the engine stops
at MaxDepth with a limit error (design section 0, R1: an input that aborts
the reference must fail the call instead).
-- with-in-else.hbs --
{{#if x}}{{else}}{{with a}}{{/if}}
-- if-in-inverse-section.hbs --
{{^x}}{{if a}}{{/x}}
-- unless-in-inverse.hbs --
{{^x}}{{unless t}}{{/x}}
-- unless-in-inverse.json --
{"t": true}
-- each-in-each-else.hbs --
{{#each xs}}{{else}}{{each a}}{{/each}}
-- if-subexpr-in-else.hbs --
{{#if x}}{{else}}{{eq (if a) ""}}{{/if}}
-- with-in-caret.hbs --
{{#if x}}{{^}}{{&with (a)}}{{/if}}
-- unless-in-with.hbs --
{{#with o}}{{unless f}}{{/with}}
-- unless-in-with.json --
{"o": {"a": 1}, "f": false}
-- equal-in-each.hbs --
{{#each a}}{{equal 1 1}}{{/each}}
-- equal-in-each.json --
{"a": [1]}
-- select-sexpr-in-if.hbs --
{{#if t}}{{to-str (select a)}}{{/if}}
-- select-sexpr-in-if.json --
{"t": true, "a": [1]}
-- if-in-if.hbs --
{{#if t}}{{if t}}{{/if}}
-- if-in-if.json --
{"t": true}
-- with-in-each.hbs --
{{#each a}}{{with t}}{{/each}}
-- with-in-each.json --
{"a": [1], "t": true}
